<title>USA: Digene Corp files for FDA ok of CMV test.</title>
<headline>Digene Corp files for FDA ok of CMV test.</headline>
<dateline>BELTSVILLE, MD. 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digene Corp said it filed with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for clearance to market its Hybrid Capture CMV DNA test in the U.S.</p>
<p>The test is aimed at diagnosing CMV infection, which causes blindness in AIDS patients and infection and death in organ transplant recipients.</p>
<p>The company said the test has an estimated worldwide market of $100 million annually.</p>
<p>The company, which makes and markets DNA testing systems, did not provide further details.</p>
<p>Officials from the company were not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
